<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dillenburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dillenburg is a town in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the Dill. Its castle, built in the 13th century, became the main residence of the Ottonian counts of Nassau, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-silent">William the Silent</a> was born there in 1533. The castle was destroyed during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a> in 1760, and only its casemates and the 19th-century William Tower remain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dillenburg.jpg" alt="Dillenburg" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Otto Domes · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dillenburg_Schlo%C3%9Fberg_Gesamtanlage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
